    "result_text": "The build is green: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`. The new `coreNumericLevel` test passes (owner with email + namesakeCount 0 \u2192 level 3).\n\nDone. The change is implemented across exactly four files, each edit small and self-contained:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `membershipTier` schema (string) with `membershipLevel` (integer 1\u20133), regenerating the DTO with `getMembershipLevel`/`setMembershipLevel`.\n- **`MembershipTier.java`** \u2014 repurposed the existing compute helper: `of(...)` now returns the numeric level (start 1, +1 for email, +1 for namesakeCount 0, capped at 3). Kept in place rather than adding/deleting files, so no extra file is touched.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 retargeted the one derivation mapping from `membershipTier` to `membershipLevel`.\n- **`RespondWithOwner.java`** \u2014 removed the `setMembershipTier(\"GOLD\")` household override (the field no longer exists), which also shrank the method.\n\nNotes on the two things the spec mentioned that turned out not to need changes:\n- **Audit line**: the create audit in `SaveOwner` records `id`/`customerCode`/`registrationDate` \u2014 it never recorded the tier, so there was nothing to convert to the level.\n- **Tenure / level 4**: reserved per the spec; not produced by creation logic, so the cap stays at 3.\n\nOne behavior change worth flagging: the old GET-path `GOLD` tier for households of \u22653 members is gone, since the spec defines the level purely from email + namesakeCount and removes the string tier field entirely. No test covered that override.",
